import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="The method — PRINCE">
  <section class="page-hero wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Prince</a><span>/</span><span>The method</span></div><span class="eyebrow">From coordinates to considered choices</span><div class="page-hero-row"><div><h1>A closer look.<br /><em>A clearer beginning.</em></h1><p class="lede">Structure first. Evidence in context. Every score, check, and source open to inspection.</p></div><a class="button" href="/workspace/">Try the workflow <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
  <div class="wrap"><section class="content-section two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / Start with what is actually there</span><h2>One target.<br /><em>The right context.</em></h2><p>Load a public PDB entry or upload a PDB/mmCIF file. Gemmi reads the coordinates, deposited author chain identifiers, residue numbers, and insertion codes.</p><p>Choose a chain and biological assembly. Assembly partners matter: a residue exposed in an isolated chain can be buried in the assembled structure.</p></div><div><h3>Check before you commit.</h3><ul class="prose-list"><li><strong>Resolvedness.</strong> Is the requested residue present in the model?</li><li><strong>Numbering.</strong> Does the chain-qualified author identifier resolve as intended?</li><li><strong>Exposure.</strong> Is the site accessible in the selected assembly?</li><li><strong>Geometry.</strong> Do the selected residues form a plausible local patch?</li></ul><div class="callout">Your chosen hotspots receive their own check. A passing proposal never replaces a STOP on the residues you selected.</div></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / Four features, nothing hidden</span><h2>A score you<br />can <em>take apart.</em></h2><p>The default antibody-epitope profile uses four features and an L2-regularized logistic-regression fit. Runtime ordering uses the signed raw dot product; the patch score is the mean of its residue scores.</p><p>The model was fit on 340 interfaces. Another 139 were reserved for validation and 110 for testing. Validation was not used for tuning.</p><a class="text-link" href="/prince/fit-protocol.json">Read the fit protocol <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="feature-table">{[
  ['Exposure','Relative solvent-accessible surface area, using FreeSASA in structural context.','+1.0756'],
  ['Concavity','A geometric feature based on local heavy-atom centroids.','−2.3035'],
  ['Hydrophobicity','Binary membership in the hydrophobic residue set.','−0.0943'],
  ['Connectivity','The exposed-residue neighborhood around each candidate.','+0.9803']
].map(([name,description,weight])=><div class="feature-row"><div><h3>{name}</h3><p>{description}</p></div><code>{weight}</code></div>)}</div></div><div class="formula">residue score = Σ (feature × fitted coefficient)<br />patch score = mean(residue scores)<small>Signed scores can be negative or greater than one. They are relative rankings, not binding probabilities. The fitted intercept is constant and omitted for ordering.</small></div></section>
  <section class="content-section two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / A source is only the beginning</span><h2>Evidence needs<br /><em>a human reading.</em></h2><p>Supply a source passage with its DOI or PMID. The local rule-based extractor drafts residue-related claims with exact quotes, character spans, and SHA-256 hashes.</p><p>Every draft begins unreviewed. Check the original source, target or homologue mapping, author numbering, assay, and direction. Reviewed rows require explicit reviewer attribution.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/#evidence">Follow the review workflow <span>↗</span></a></div><div><h3>Keep the distinction visible.</h3><ul class="prose-list"><li><strong>Structural observations</strong> describe coordinates and structural context.</li><li><strong>Reviewed functional assays and mutagenesis</strong> can qualify for evidence-first ordering.</li><li><strong>Support and refutation</strong> remain visible. Conflicting coverage cancels in the evidence-score numerator.</li><li><strong>Original structural rank and score</strong> remain attached after evidence ordering.</li></ul><div class="callout warning-callout">Evidence-first ranking uses reviewed functional evidence. Its effect on predictive performance remains unevaluated.</div></div></section>
  <section class="content-section two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / Take the reasoning with you</span><h2>A result.<br /><em>And its receipts.</em></h2><p>Export the complete JSON run record, a CSV containing proposed sites and independent selected-hotspot checks, or unreviewed draft YAML for later review.</p></div><div><h3>Using the result</h3><p>GO records passing structural checks. The model ranks sites using antibody-contact labels; experimental accessibility and affinity require assays.</p><p>Read each finding, compare the evidence, and use PRINCE as one input to a research decision.</p><a class="text-link" href="/validation/">See the measured results <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
  <div class="inline-cta"><h2>Have a target <em>in mind?</em></h2><a class="button" href="/workspace/">Find your starting point <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
</Layout>
